<p>The forecast for more bad weather finally did it and the Waterford Homes Tour and Crafts Exhibit (otherwise known to everyone in Loudoun County as the Waterford Fair) was cancelled. Some of the activities have been rescheduled as a new event on October 17 &amp; 18: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/events/1199204360094829/1199590620056203/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Waterford Art Harvest</a>. This event will be free and open to the public.</p>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>
<div><span style="line-height: 1.42857;">In place of the art show that is normally held there will be a show of the Art Exhibit paintings in the old school building. Additionally, the Art Mart will also be open at the Schooley Mill Barn on Janney Street (behind the Second Street School).&nbsp;</span><span style="line-height: 1.42857;">I have work in both parts of the event.</span></div>
</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>In other news, there is a Loudoun Sketch Club art show upcoming at Aldie Mill. This will be open on October 10, 11, 12 and during the <a href="http://www.villageofaldie.com/harvestfest.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Aldie Festival</a>, October 16, 17, so please stop by and see what's for sale if you are in the area.</div>